  "causal_contrasts": {
    "recording": "fixed0_record/fixed0_off and fixed32_record/fixed32_off include router atomics and native window copy/reset; map and no-migration policy fixed",
    "mapping_and_bookkeeping": "fixed0_off/OFF includes map kernel, prepare_forward and native step; cannot uniquely attribute to one without profile/replay",
    "replica_capacity": "fixed32_off/fixed0_off changes32extra slots, ownership and expert work, not a pure memory allocation cost",
    "replica_layout": "balanced32_off/fixed32_off holds32extra copies and native hash dispatch, changes placement AND which logical experts are replicated",
    "dispatcher": "resident_v2/balanced32_off uses same resident map but also removes native per-step state; not a pure mapper-only contrast"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "One eight-request pilot group, fixed sequential arm order; no uncertainty or unique causal decomposition of every timing delta.",
    "Equal output counts do not force token/routing identity. LongBench timings vary widely and do not show a consistent recording penalty.",
    "B4_light retains original-history shadow and is excluded from cost timing contrasts.",
    "NCCL kernel durations include rank arrival skew, peer waiting and synchronization. Collective replay removes expert compute but remains a component benchmark, not wire-time proof.",
    "The proposed packed optimization applies to OFF too; any general transport benefit must not be attributed to the stability gate or resident dispatch policy."
  ],
